|CKOThieves are specialists in information, access, and unfair timing.
Case a mark, create Opportunity through meaningful setup, then spend
it on control, poison, escape, or a prepared finish.

Thief uses automatic Guild XP advancement, not carried gold. Battle
contribution, successful jobs, and meaningful combat practice grant
GXP. Combat practice grants about 5 GXP no more than once every
10-14 seconds against a suitable foe. Ranks 1 through 20 open
the command kit; uncapped ranks beyond that support utility and
reliability progression. Every rank grants a Knack point.

Start with:

  |BKBtstatus|CKO        Rank, GXP, Opportunity, study, incident, poison
  |BKBknacks|CKO         Ghost, Grifter, and Knife customization
  |BKBcase <target>|CKO  Study one mark and gain two Opportunity
  |BKBdirtyfight ...|CKO Spend Opportunity on an unfair opening
  |BKBtpowers|CKO        Complete command and unlock listing

The world kit uses bounded theft and ordinary movement contracts. Pilfer
and Pick reject protected items, coin theft takes only a fraction, Slip
and Vanish travel through real exits, and Shadow can be noticed. Pressure
traps can catch stationary enemies in combat and can be poison-laced.

Thieves use the common Bleeding and Exposed conditions, so other
guilds and party members can build openings for them. Weapon attacks
do not require daggers or a particular damage type; the normal guild
equipment allow/restrict rules still apply.

A landed Quick Strike against the Studied mark has a 60% chance to
find Opportunity. Directly establishing a fresh Bleeding, Exposed,
Blind, Concentration disruption, or movement block finds another.

Read |BKB'thelp revival'|CKO for the complete system overview,
|BKB'thelp poison'|CKO for poisoncraft, and |BKB'thelp rules'|CKO
for guild conduct.
